#block(breakable: false)[*Rebuilding the environment.* On AWS, five clean rebuilds between 17 October and 11 November took 30 min 59 s to 33 min 47 s (@tbl-delivery-timings, §5.3), above the 30 min target (AISS-06). On 14 November we ran V8 R4 by hand rather than through the workflow. It rebuilt the environment in 29 min 54 s with every readiness, health and smoke check in place; we then destroyed the new runtime and confirmed it was gone (§5.3). R1–R3 failed. With 6 s to spare and five earlier rebuilds over the target, we read this as one pass at the recorded configuration, not a reliable recovery time. A rebuild restores service, not data, and it gives no service during a zone loss.]
